  "basis": "The task requires selecting the highest-risk state from the provided options based on the state risk dashboard. The dashboard is a choropleth map where color encodes risk index: dark red = highest risk (80-100), orange = medium risk (20-60), and light yellow = lowest risk (0-20). The options are limited to Illinois (IL), Kansas (KS), and Delaware (DE). According to the chart, Kansas (KS) is colored dark red, indicating a risk index of 80-100. Illinois (IL) is colored light yellow, indicating a risk index of 0-20. Delaware (DE) is colored orange, indicating a risk index of 20-60. Under the shared legend, dark red represents the highest risk level. Therefore, Kansas (KS) is the highest-risk state among the options.",
